course: dictionary
lesson: 2011
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word condition is a good example. «The bike is in good condition, with new brakes.» Here condition means the state something is in.
explain: «Plants need the right conditions to grow, so in a fair test we keep the light and water the same.» Here conditions means the surroundings, like light and temperature. Ask yourself which meaning fits best, then swap it in for the word and read the sentence again.
explain: «You can borrow the bike on condition that you wear a helmet.» Here condition means a rule that must be followed first. The words on condition that are a clue: they set a rule. A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Condition is a noun, and its plural is conditions.
fact: «Condition» can mean the state something is in, such as good, bad, new or broken.
fact: «Condition» can mean something that must happen before another thing can happen.
fact: «Condition» can mean an illness or health problem that lasts a long time.
fact: «Conditions» can mean the situation around you, like weather conditions or living conditions.
exercise: «A rental deposit comes back if the home is left in good condition.» In this sentence, what does condition mean? | *The state the home is in | A rule that must happen first | The weather outside | An illness that lasts a long time
exercise: «Many classmates live with long-term conditions, such as epilepsy.» What does condition mean here? | The state of a bike | The weather outside | A rule about borrowing | *An illness or health problem that lasts a long time
exercise: «Ella can go to the park on condition that she is home by six.» What do the words on condition that mean? | The weather is good | *Only if a rule is kept first | Very quickly | Without any clothes
test: «Plants need the right conditions to grow.» Conditions here means | *The surroundings, like light and water | A type of puppy | A bag of seeds | A hospital
test: «Some puppies come from puppy farms where mothers are kept in poor conditions.» What does conditions mean here? | A long journey | A rule for buying a puppy | A kind of food | *The living situation around them
exam: Which meaning of condition fits best in «Please check the condition of the tyres before the trip»? | *The state the tyres are in | An illness that lasts a long time | A rule that must happen first | Living conditions
